      "q": "3. For the following A.P.s, write the first term and the common difference.\n$$\\mathbf{3},\\mathbf{1},-\\mathbf{1},-\\mathbf{3},...$$",
      "a": "From the given AP, we can see that the first term is $3$.\nThe common difference is the difference between any two consecutive numbers of the A.P.\nCommon difference $=$ ${{2}^{nd}}\\text{ }term-{{1}^{st}}\\ term$\n$\\therefore $ Common difference $=$ $1-3=-2$.\n$$-5,-1,3,7,...$$\nAns:\nFrom the given AP, we can see that the first term is $-5$.\nThe common difference is the difference between any two consecutive numbers of the A.P.\nCommon difference $=$ ${{2}^{nd}}\\text{ }term-{{1}^{st}}\\ term$\n$\\therefore $ Common difference $=$ $-1-\\left( -5 \\right)=4$.\n$$\\dfrac{1}{3}\\text{,}\\dfrac{5}{3}\\text{,}\\dfrac{9}{3}\\text{,}\\dfrac{13}{3},...$$\nAns:\nFrom the given AP, we can see that the first term is $\\dfrac{1}{3}$.\nThe common difference is the difference between any two consecutive numbers of the A.P.\nCommon difference $=$ ${{2}^{nd}}\\text{ }term-{{1}^{st}}\\ term$\n$\\therefore $ Common difference $=$ $\\dfrac{5}{3}-\\dfrac{1}{3}=\\dfrac{4}{3}$.\n$$0.6,1.7,2.8,3.9,...$$\nAns:\nFrom the given AP, we can see that the first term is $0.6$.\nThe common difference is the difference between any two consecutive numbers of the A.P.\nCommon difference $=$ ${{2}^{nd}}\\text{ }term-{{1}^{st}}\\ term$\n$\\therefore $ Common difference $=$ $1.7-0.6=1.1$."
